## Required outcome and mechanism

The rejected package `5547224fe805c932f258e213c453c285d40feeec` queried only
main.sqlite_master. A connection-local TEMP trigger on main.cards can therefore
write an unrelated audit table while every original freshness/postcondition
check succeeds. A trigger installed immediately before the native batch has
the same effect. Independent red source and both original native observations
are preserved without alteration in registered ignored
`.runtime/members-key-effective-schema-20261031/original-independent-red/`.

Recovery must refuse unreviewed effective instrumentation and late schema
changes without changing recovery or custom-table data. Missing metadata is
an error, not an empty schema. IDs, authored contents, history, original 0006
ledger, collision refusals and no-replay semantics remain intact. A batch must
not acknowledge a committed repair that an enclosing caller transaction can
later undo. That caller-transaction composition was explicitly unsupported in
the rejected package; this patch mechanically enforces the boundary rather
than treating the retained outside-contract observation as another corruption.

