## Effective-schema qualification

All recovery reads and mutations explicitly address main tables. Both complete
main and TEMP catalogs are bound to the reviewed plan and first SQL assertion
inside the same native atomic mutation batch, including views and implicit
indexes. JSON encoding preserves definition boundaries. The planner refuses
all pre-existing TEMP objects, rather than guessing which are harmless.

The native read-only pragma_table_list() metadata includes an sqlite_schema
entry even for an empty attached database. Its complete ordered projection is
also bound to the plan and atomic assertion. All schemas other than main and
temp are refused, including attachments with retained data. Function-call
syntax fails if a real table shadows that metadata name. Missing, malformed,
unauthorized or inconsistent metadata throws. There is no authorization-error
fallback. The assertion independently requires no TEMP object and no attached
schema even if a planner read were interrupted by a metadata change.

Known cards/reference freshness triggers write deck_data_version, so additional
triggers on that table are also unreviewed effects. The six existing required
trigger bodies remain exact. Unrelated history-table freshness triggers are
not classified as effects of this repair; all their definitions are still
bound by the complete schema stamp. Foreign keys retain native
PRAGMA main.foreign_key_list qualification. A view, trigger, foreign key, TEMP
object or attachment appearing immediately before batch execution fails before
the key/reference writes. The existing final key/reference/version assertion
remains in that batch.

Local workerd D1 supports both catalog reads and pragma_table_list(), while
database_list, TEMP creation and ATTACH are authorization failures. Those D1
restrictions remain enabled and have actual negative controls. No D1 guard was
removed to make metadata work.

## Caller-owned transaction admission

SQLStatement gains opt-in requireStandaloneTransaction; the driver guarantee
standaloneBatchAdmission must positively advertise support. Recovery requires
that guarantee and marks its first statement. Existing ordinary batches keep
their nesting behavior.

LocalSqliteDriver examines every batch input and its actual native connection's
inTransaction state before starting any statement. That synchronous check and
native batch execution have no asynchronous gap. It rejects both transaction()
composition and a caller's direct SQL BEGIN, including admission immediately
before batch execution. CloudflareD1Adapter rejects the marked batch while its
own compensating transaction is active, before its lease/statement execution.
The unchanged schema guard also excludes journal instrumentation installed by
another D1 transaction. Unsupported adapters refuse before planning.

Admission errors during apply retain the conservative outcome-unconfirmed
classification and original cause. No automatic retry, inverse mutation or
acknowledgement-based cleanup was added. A no-op reports observed state and
does not submit a mutation batch.

